---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Research | Shabel Lab">
    <section class="page-header">
        <h1>Our Research</h1>
    </section>

    <section class="projects-container">
        
        <!-- Project 1 Summary -->
        <article class="project-card">
            <!-- Placeholder for a diagram or microscopy image -->
            <div class="project-image">
                <img src="/images/rawfp.jpg" alt="Microscopy diagram showing neural circuitry of affective bias" />
            </div>
            
            <div class="project-content">
                <h2>Neural Mechanisms of Affective Bias</h2>
                <p>We developed a behavioral test for optimism and pessimism in mice and are using it to understand the molecular, synaptic, and circuit signaling mechanisms of affective bias.</p>
                <!-- This links to the sub-page we are about to create! -->
                <a href="/research/affective-bias" class="read-more-btn">Read More &rarr;</a>
            </div>
        </article>

        <!-- Project 2 Summary -->
        <article class="project-card">
            <div class="project-image">
                <img src="/images/colabelingcover.png" alt="colabeling for synaptic mechanism of reinforcement signals" />
            </div>

            <div class="project-content">
                <h2>A Synaptic Mechanism for Creating and Diversifying Reinforcement Signals</h2>
                <p>We discovered glutamate/GABA co-release in the habenula and found that it is a potential mechanism for creating and diversifying reinforcement signals in the brain.</p>
                <a href="/research/a-synaptic-mechanism-for-creating-and-diversifying-reinforcement-signals" class="read-more-btn">Read More &rarr;</a>
            </div>
        </article>

        <!-- Project 3 Summary -->
        <article class="project-card">
            <div class="project-image">
                <img src="/images/gpr151cover.jpg" alt="gpr151 for depression-enriched circuit therapeutic" />
            </div>

            <div class="project-content">
                <h2>A Depression-Circuit Enriched GPCR for Targeted Pharmacotherapy</h2>
                <p>We identified GPR151, an orphan G protein-coupled receptor that is exceptionally enriched in the habenula, as a candidate therapeutic target for inflammation-associated depression.</p>
                <a href="/research/a-depression-circuit-enriched-GPCR-for-targeted-pharmacotherapy" class="read-more-btn">Read More &rarr;</a>
            </div>
        </article>

        <!-- Project 4 Summary -->
        <article class="project-card">
            <div class="project-image">
                <img src="/images/MDDCover.png" alt="Microscopy showing green channel cells" />
            </div>

            <div class="project-content">
                <h2>The Functional Organization of The Lateral Habenula and its Relationship to MDD (Depression)</h2>
                <p>We are mapping the functional heterogeneity of habenula neurons to their molecular identities and cell-type-specific projection targets to understand the phenotypes of habenula neurons that are altered in depression.</p>
                <a href="/research/the-functional-organization-of-the-lateral-habenula-and-its-relationship-to-MDD" class="read-more-btn">Read More &rarr;</a>
            </div>
        </article>

    </section>
</Layout>

<style>
    .page-header {
        text-align: center;
        margin-bottom: 4rem;
    }

    .page-header h1 {
        color: var(--primary-color);
        font-size: 2.5rem;
        margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    }

    .page-header p {
        color: var(--text-muted);
        max-width: 600px;
        margin: 0 auto;
        font-size: 1.1rem;
    }

    .projects-container {
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        gap: 3rem; /* Space between each project card */
    }

    .project-card {
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        background-color: #ffffff;
        border-radius: 8px;
        overflow: hidden;
        box-shadow: 0 4px 6px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);
        transition: box-shadow 0.2s ease;
    }

    .project-card:hover {
        box-shadow: 0 8px 15px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);
    }

    /* On screens wider than 768px (tablets/desktops), put image and text side-by-side */
    @media (min-width: 768px) {
        .project-card {
            flex-direction: row;
        }
    }

    .project-image {
        flex: 1;
        min-height: 250px;
        /* REMOVED the gray background and opacity */
        overflow: hidden; /* Keeps the image strictly inside its bounds */
    }

    /* NEW: Styles the image to perfectly fill the container */
    .project-image img {
        width: 100%;
        height: 100%;
        object-fit: cover; /* Acts like a background image: fills the space without squishing */
        display: block;
    }

    .project-content {
        flex: 2;
        padding: 2.5rem;
        display: flex;
        flex-direction: column;
        justify-content: center;
        align-items: flex-start; /* Keeps the button aligned to the left */
    }

    .project-content h2 {
        color: var(--primary-color);
        margin-top: 0;
        margin-bottom: 1rem;
        font-size: 1.8rem;
    }

    .project-content p {
        margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
        font-size: 1.05rem;
    }

    .read-more-btn {
        background-color: var(--primary-color);
        color: #ffffff;
        padding: 0.75rem 1.5rem;
        text-decoration: none;
        border-radius: 4px;
        font-weight: 600;
        transition: background-color 0.2s ease;
    }

    .read-more-btn:hover {
        background-color: #00366b; /* A slightly darker shade of UTSW blue for the hover state */
    }

    /* ========================================== */
    /* MOBILE RESPONSIVENESS FIXES                */
    /* ========================================== */
    @media (max-width: 768px) {
        .page-header {
            margin-bottom: 2rem; /* Reduces dead space below the title */
        }

        .page-header h1 {
            font-size: 2rem; /* Scales down the title */
        }

        .projects-container {
            gap: 1.5rem; /* Reduces the massive gap between stacked project cards */
        }

        .project-image {
            min-height: 200px; /* Makes the images slightly shorter so they don't dominate the screen */
        }

        .project-content {
            padding: 1.5rem; /* Cuts the padding almost in half so text has room to breathe */
        }

        .project-content h2 {
            font-size: 1.4rem; /* Shrinks the project titles so they fit on the screen better */
        }
    }
</style>